{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cacf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a809-8791-7622-9a9b-78a086ec7f4f"},"sequence":962,"recorded_at":1780531400001919,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8b868cf4-3c1a-4266-acd2-1e63eb0638f1","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8b868cf4-3c1a-4266-acd2-1e63eb0638f1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8b868cf4-3c1a-4266-acd2-1e63eb0638f1"},"call_id":"call_01a0a8126de87553a29729a95248dbb7","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-08-30\n7|\n8|### Shared-runtime Story landing gates recovered (TASK-260830-1x524u)\n9|\n10|- INTEGRITY: The five Shared Runtime Story checkpoint commits were re-materialized with valid configured-human signatures and monotonic Asia/Tbilisi timestamps. Local and remote `task-board/story/STORY-260715-1y04r0` now match at `9bf4d0892db03035b989a4c040cfee37636ff8df`; all prior Story children and the direct packet-bridge, SSH-engine, and generated-project architecture blockers are terminal.\n11|- LANDING GATES: The candidate preserves the existing serial Codex/Sol high spawn policy and adds the fail-closed `make credential-free-validate` Story integration suite. The owning Epic dependency was narrowed to the accepted macOS architecture verification. Scoped board reads show this Task and Story unblocked with every prior direct child terminal; the current board-wide validator returns exit `0` while reporting 368 `MISSING_ACTIVITY` records outside the current Task/Story streams, so the handoff preserves that anomaly instead of backfilling transaction-owned activity or claiming a globally clean board.\n12|- BOUNDARY: Revalidation changes no runtime behavior and does not add live provider wiring. The generated macOS `PacketTunnelProvider` remains a lifecycle shell; validation is limited to deterministic harnesses, compile/build gates, documentation, and read-only system-state observations, with no provider launch, VPN activation, route mutation, or DNS mutation.\n13|- VALIDATION REWORK: The first configured completion attempt failed closed because the managed worktree resolved the default sibling legacy checkout inside `.temp`; its command now derives the control repository through Git's absolute common directory. The next attempt exposed a stale “valid” scheme fixture that omitted the two UI-test schemes already required by the production exact-set gate; the fixture and all isolated missing/unexpected rows now use the complete active graph. Narrowing the production gate by only `ReluxProxyIOSUITests` makes the named contract test exit `1`; byte-identical restoration returns it to `0`.\n14|- FINAL EVIDENCE: The corrected credential-free completion suite, eight focused runtime suites (105 tests), six harness tests plus seven fixtures, 32 M0 binding negatives, both platform adapter builds, unsigned macOS targets, 52 local documentation links, and four byte-identical PlantUML SVG renders pass. The full 514-test/44-suite Swift run passes with the 25 explicitly unavailable ReluxNIOSSH rows; selected Shared Runtime/M1 coverage is 90.34% lines and 84.33% regions, and package coverage is 92.92% lines and 85.22% regions.\n15|- PRIVACY OBSERVATION: Broad route-table hashes changed during long build runs and are retained as inconclusive dynamic-state evidence, not a pass. A bounded route-socket monitor around a fresh production-entry harness run recorded 35 `RTM_MISS` lookup events and zero `RTM_ADD`, `RTM_DELETE`, `RTM_CHANGE`, `RTM_NEWADDR`, or `RTM_DELADDR` mutations; full-tunnel route selectors, NetworkExtension configuration, DNS state, and the zero Relux process set matched before and after.\n16|\n17|### Accepted M0 production bindings (TASK-260720-1qhxqa)\n18|\n19|- DECISION: Bound the exact reviewer-accepted generated-project, packet/HEV, and SSH outcome/verdict resource pairs plus the accepted M1 runtime contract in `Configuration/TASK-260720-1qhxqa_m0-production-bindings-v1.json`. Acceptance timestamps preserve upstream date precision instead of inventing a time of day.\n20|- PERMIT: `productionCompositionPermitted=true` is only a recomputed result. `scripts/validate-m0-production-bindings.py` fails closed on digest drift, absence, malformed input, unknown schema/fields, stale/superseded evidence, a narrowed input set, negative/missing compatibility rows, and checked-in graph/native-pin drift.\n21|- BINDINGS: macOS-only generated graph; MTU/buffers/batching/HEV values 1500/32768/64/5ms/24576/4096/2/500 with no HEV fork; selected pinned libssh2/OpenSSL adapter with exact algorithm, window, rekey, lifecycle, notice, maintenance, and revalidation constraints. Deferred iOS, MTU 4096/8500, whole-extension memory, general UDP, lanes, reconnect, and M3 tuning remain blocked/deferred.\n22|- CONSUMER: `TASK-260715-3ejhyy` must use the machine manifest as its sole M0 binding source and validate it at the future macOS production factory entry point before concrete SSH/PacketFlowBridge/HEV construction or `NetworkSettingsApplier.apply`.\n23|- BOARD ANOMALY: Final `task-board validate` returned process exit 0 but printed two `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` rows. `STORY-260715-2ungml` is unrelated; current `STORY-260715-1y04r0` remained `backlog` while this leaf was `development`. The leaf had `derivedBlockedBy=[]`, all four hard prerequisites were `done`, and the manifest/resource gates passed. The mismatch is retained as board-state evidence rather than misreported as a clean board validation.\n24|- REVIEW REWORK: CR revision 1 was correctly rejected because the validator admitted a mutant with MTU 1501, packet budget 1, removed notice obligations, and an `unchecked` compatibility condition. The rework pins SHA-256 `fda46421ae6a6c24cf58f5bfb520399b9ebc8d31800b7d61ed18a3823